{
  "name": "lockers",
  "about": "A town founded by its host has its lockers where the host places them: a Librarian with no locker isn't one the Merchant manages, and once its locker stands at a workstation (a Locker point, tied to it) it is. The locker's chests are counted with the town's: the paper a player left there is the town's, carried to the desk's chests at once (Moved out of the locker, into the desk). The screen switches the Librarian's paper trade on; two days on its locker has sold the town's paper, two trades a restock while the paper lasts, and the Librarian and the Merchant earned their XP (HandLevel). Untied, the locker isn't managed. A locker at a point that isn't one is refused; a switch for a hand or an offer that isn't there is ignored. Saved and loaded, the lockers are as they were.",
